513
00:28:09,940 --> 00:28:13,820
但车的其余部分，
我实在是找不出半点有趣的地方。
but with the rest of the car,
I was struggling to find
something interesting.

514
00:28:15,820 --> 00:28:18,700
-奥迪这转向灯的嗒嗒声质感真好。
-[女孩轻笑]
-Good quality indicator tick
in Audis.
-[GIRL CHUCKLES]

515
00:28:18,740 --> 00:28:23,420
不过这版本最烦人的地方，
就是那细碎颠簸的行驶质感。
The most irritating thing
on this version, though,
was the choppy ride.

516
00:28:23,460 --> 00:28:25,180
自然，
不是所有人都赞同。
Naturally,
not everyone agreed.

517
00:28:25,220 --> 00:28:29,260
在同等价位下，这车的替代选择，
当然就是SE版。
The alternative to this one,
of course, at a similar price,
is the SE.

518
00:28:29,300 --> 00:28:30,980
-而我……
-换作是我就会买那个！
-And I...
-Which is the one
I would have!

519
00:28:31,020 --> 00:28:32,660
我才不买。
I wouldn't.

520
00:28:32,700 --> 00:28:37,260
好啦，现在刚过凌晨两点，
Right. It is just gone 2:00
in the morning,

521
00:28:37,300 --> 00:28:42,500
我还得再测一辆。不过首先，
我得把我的自行车拼好。
and I've got another one
to do. But first,
I've gotta build my bike.

522
00:28:43,340 --> 00:28:45,020
呵，真是让人“开心”。
Oh, joy.

523
00:28:45,060 --> 00:28:49,020
至于心直口快的梅先生呢？
呵，这回他算是踢到铁板了。
And the blunt Mr May?
Well, he'd met his match.

524
00:28:49,060 --> 00:28:52,660
呃，我搞到了她的电话号码，
随时可以打给她，
Well, I got her phone number,
so I can always
give her a ring

525
00:28:52,700 --> 00:28:54,940
要是我后面的其他公路测试卡壳的话。
if I get stuck on any
of my other road tests.

526
00:28:56,540 --> 00:28:59,740
是啊，詹姆斯，
你表现太棒了！
Yes, James,
you were very good!

527
00:29:00,540 --> 00:29:02,580
简直无可挑剔。
You were marvellous.

528
00:29:03,220 --> 00:29:04,900
你……
You...

529
00:29:06,380 --> 00:29:08,940
-你简直逊爆了！
-什么？哎……
-You were pathetic!
-What? Well...

530
00:29:08,980 --> 00:29:13,140
还扯什么不忍心告诉别人
他们的车有多烂，全是废话。
Just all that rubbish about
not wanting to tell people
how bad their cars were.

531
00:29:13,180 --> 00:29:14,860
好吧，我当时确实有那么点……
火气冲了点。
All right, I was a bit...
Peppery.

532
00:29:16,180 --> 00:29:18,540
对啊，呃……因为说实话，喷车根本一点都不难。
Yes, um... 'Cause it's not
difficult, frankly.

533
00:29:18,580 --> 00:29:22,420
我是说，他不就证明了这点吗？
比如你，台下的，你开什么车？
I mean, he proved it, okay?
I mean, for instance,
what do you drive?

534
00:29:22,460 --> 00:29:24,660
-一辆SD1。
-罗孚SD1？
-An SD1.
-A Rover SD1?

535
00:29:24,700 --> 00:29:27,620
你看，那就是辆烂车。
You see, that's an awful car.

536
00:29:27,660 --> 00:29:29,140
-你呢，你开什么车？
-雷诺Clio。
-You, what have you got?
-A Renault Clio.

537
00:29:29,180 --> 00:29:32,020
偷来的吧，干得漂亮。
You stole that, good.

538
00:29:32,060 --> 00:29:35,020
当年就是雷诺Clio这辆车，
让我毅然离开了老版《Top Gear》，
Renault Clio was the car
that caused me
to leave old Top Gear

539
00:29:35,060 --> 00:29:38,260
因为那车实在太无聊了，
无聊到我都不知道该说什么好。
'cause it was so boring,
I couldn't think of anything
to say about it.

540
00:29:38,300 --> 00:29:41,780
-看吧，喷车有多容易？
-喂，你，给我出来。
-See how easy this is?
-Oi, you, come out here.

541
00:29:41,820 --> 00:29:44,900
问问他！
问问他开的是什么！
Ask him!
Ask him what he's got!

542
00:29:44,940 --> 00:29:47,860
我开福特嘉年华。
我有辆嘉年华。
I've got a Fiesta.
I've got a Fiesta.

543
00:29:47,900 --> 00:29:49,900
-大块头，那你觉得那车怎么样？
-挺好的车。
-What do you think
of that then, big fella?
-Good car.

544
00:29:49,940 --> 00:29:52,180
-瞧见没。
-你说啥？再说一遍？
-There you go.
-You what? Sorry?

545
00:29:52,220 --> 00:29:54,300
-我是坐在后排开的！
-你坐后座开？
-I drive it
from the back seat!
-You drive from the back seat.

546
00:29:54,340 --> 00:29:57,460
这也太吓人了！
我觉得……我觉得……
This is terrifying!
I feel like... I feel like...

547
00:29:57,500 --> 00:30:01,140
你见过巨石阵顶上的横梁
往下砸的样子吗？
Have you ever seen Stonehenge
when the top bits drop off?

548
00:30:01,180 --> 00:30:06,100
不过说真的，
你载的那个奥迪女车主，
简直太神了。
I've got to say, though,
that Audi woman you had,
she was amazing.

549
00:30:06,140 --> 00:30:11,020
是啊，我莫名觉得她
特别有魅力。
Yeah, I found her
strangely attractive.

550
00:30:11,060 --> 00:30:13,380
这有什么好莫名的，
人家本来就很迷人。
Nothing strange about the
attraction there.
She was great.

551
00:30:13,420 --> 00:30:16,420
言归正传，最后问一句，
那个折叠踏板车贵不贵？
Now before I finish,
that scooter, then,
was it expensive?

552
00:30:16,460 --> 00:30:19,940
呃，算下来其实差不多就等于
打车回趟家，
Um, well, it works out about
the same as, you know,
a taxi trip home

553
00:30:19,980 --> 00:30:23,140
然后第二天再打车去酒吧
把车接回家的费用，所以……
and then one back to get
your car to take it home
from the pub, so...

554
00:30:23,180 --> 00:30:25,460
那你们俩把钱花哪儿去了？
So what did you two do
with your money?

555
00:30:25,500 --> 00:30:30,060
我们喝得烂醉如泥，然后掏钱
雇了个骑小踏板的傻帽来接我们。
We got drunk and then paid
for some berk on a scooter
to come and pick us up.

556
00:30:30,100 --> 00:30:34,780
好了，现在又到了
把明星请进廉价车跑圈的时间。
Okay, it is now time
to put a star
in our reasonably-priced car.

557
00:30:34,820 --> 00:30:37,260
他是一位名声大噪的DJ、
He's a hugely successful DJ,

558
00:30:37,300 --> 00:30:40,380
电视节目主持人，也是位成功的商人。
television presenter
and businessman.

559
00:30:40,420 --> 00:30:45,460
而他能在取得这一切成就的前提，
是他生来就饱受一种可怕天疾的折磨——
And he achieved all this
despite being born
with a terrible affliction.

560
00:30:47,100 --> 00:30:48,940
红头发。
Ginger hair.

561
00:30:48,980 --> 00:30:51,660
女士们先生们，
克里斯·埃文斯！
Ladies and gentlemen,
Chris Evans!

562
00:30:54,740 --> 00:30:56,220
-最近怎么样，老兄？
-见到你真高兴。
-How are you, mate?
-Nice to see you.

563
00:30:56,260 --> 00:30:59,060
-我也很高兴见到你。
坐吧。
-你还好吧？
-Good to see you.
Have a seat.
-You okay?

564
00:31:06,940 --> 00:31:09,100
-话说，你要回电台做节目了。
-没错。
-Now, you're going back
on the radio.
-I am.

565
00:31:09,140 --> 00:31:11,100
-BBC广播二台。
-好像是，
我也是这么听说的。
-Radio 2.
-Apparently.
That's what I heard.

566
00:31:11,140 --> 00:31:13,860
-那可是个大台啊，
巨头云集之地。
-确实。
-That's the big one.
Land of the giants.
-Yup.

567
00:31:13,900 --> 00:31:17,260
-沃根、罗斯、布鲁斯……
现在又加上了你。
-嗯哼。
-Wogan, Ross, Bruce...
And now you.
-Uh-huh.

568
00:31:17,300 --> 00:31:19,820
-你去那儿凑什么热闹？
-你这话什么意思？
-What're you doing there?
-What does that mean?

569
00:31:19,860 --> 00:31:22,660
巨头云集之地，
广播界的大腕们……
Land of the giants,
the giants in broadcasting...

570
00:31:22,700 --> 00:31:24,620
-你紧张吗？
-不，一点都不。
-Are you nervous about it?
-No. Not at all.

571
00:31:24,660 --> 00:31:26,060
-真的？
-真的不紧张。
-Really?
-No.

572
00:31:26,100 --> 00:31:27,580
我就是吃这碗饭的。
你现在紧张吗？
It's what I do for a living.
Are you nervous now?

573
00:31:27,620 --> 00:31:29,740
-不紧张。
-那你可就该紧张了，宝贝！
-No.
-Well, you should be, baby!

574
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:33,600
完全不慌，放松得很。
节目什么时候播？
Absolutely not, completely relaxed.
When's the show gonna be on?

575
00:31:33,620 --> 00:31:38,020
九月。周六下午两点到五点。
绝对是一档超棒的开车伴随节目。（可不像TG第23季）
September. Saturday afternoons, 2-5.
A really good driving show. (unlike TG S23)

576
00:31:38,040 --> 00:31:40,180
是啊，因为你巴不得听众
都困在车里，对吧？
Yeah, 'cause you like the audience
to be in the car, don't you?

577
00:31:40,600 --> 00:31:44,600
这样他们就成了“被扣押的听众”，
想跑都跑不掉。
Well, it's like a captive audience then.
They can't really get away.

578
00:31:45,780 --> 00:31:49,020
而且二台还有个毛病，
一到晚上七点
节目就全歇菜了。
The other thing as well,
about Radio 2 is it
always finishes at 7:00.

579
00:31:49,060 --> 00:31:51,660
-你注意到了没？
-怎么，七点之后
就啥都没了？
-You noticed that?
-What, there's nowt on
after that.

580
00:31:51,700 --> 00:31:53,620
对啊，啥都没了，
放的全是民谣之类的玩意儿。
Yeah, there's nothing on.
It's folk or something.

581
00:31:53,660 --> 00:31:55,740
所以你就切到广播四台，
结果一转过去，
就是《阿切尔一家》。
So you turn to Radio 4
and then
you've got The Archers.

582
00:31:55,780 --> 00:31:58,540
对，而且我不得不说，
《阿切尔一家》根本就……
Yeah, which I've got to say
The Archers is not...

583
00:31:58,580 --> 00:32:01,180
因为我也住在村里……
我们村里的事儿可比《阿切尔一家》刺激多了。
'Cause I live in a village...
Our village is far more
exciting than The Archers.

584
00:32:01,220 --> 00:32:03,220
而且《阿切尔一家》里搞什么女同接吻……
谁想听那个啊。
And the lesbian kiss
on The Archers...
You don't want that.

585
00:32:03,260 --> 00:32:05,140
大家想听的是巨型蔬菜评比。
You want the giant vegetables.

586
00:32:05,180 --> 00:32:07,500
-那才是地道的乡村生活。
-女同接吻？
-'Cause that's the real deal.
-A lesbian kiss?

587
00:32:07,540 --> 00:32:08,860
-女同接吻。
-在广播里？！
-A lesbian kiss.
-On the radio?

588
00:32:08,900 --> 00:32:12,020
-对啊，我是说，如果你……
-这玩意儿在广播里怎么播得出来？
-Yeah, I mean, if you...
-How does that work?

589
00:32:12,060 --> 00:32:15,260
呃，根本播不出来，
反正对我来说完全不行。
但你看，真正的乡村大戏……
Well, it doesn't work,
obviously not for me.
But you know, real drama...

590
00:32:15,300 --> 00:32:17,180
呃，其实还是能……[结巴]
Well, it does... [STAMMERS]

591
00:32:18,860 --> 00:32:20,980
不过，嗯，村里真正的戏码
其实是这样的……
But, um, no, real drama
in villages is like...

592
00:32:21,020 --> 00:32:23,180
你看，我们村里有个家伙
人称“鸡蛋艾伦”，对吧？
You know, We've got this guy
called Alan The Egg, right?

593
00:32:23,220 --> 00:32:26,060
他一年能卖出
两万四千打鸡蛋。
Who actually sells 24,000
dozen eggs every year.

594
00:32:26,100 --> 00:32:30,500
我们村还有另一个家伙
叫“鼹鼠艾伦”，
是个专门抓害兽的灭害工。
We've also got this other guy
called Alan The Mole
who's a pest exterminator.

595
00:32:30,540 --> 00:32:34,060
我以前经常跟“鼹鼠艾伦”打交道，
因为我家地里闹鼹鼠。
Now, I used to deal with
Alan The Mole because I had
some moles on me land.

596
00:32:34,100 --> 00:32:36,940
后来我去酒馆，有人就问我：
“哎，你见过‘鸡蛋艾伦’了没？”
And so I used to go in the pub
and they said, "Oh, have you
met Alan The Egg yet?"

597
00:32:36,980 --> 00:32:39,620
没见过。我还琢磨：“村里既有个‘鼹鼠艾伦’，
又有个‘鸡蛋艾伦’，不觉得很奇怪吗？”
No. I thought, "Isn't it weird
there's an Alan The Mole
and an Alan The Egg?"

598
00:32:39,660 --> 00:32:41,100
结果他娘的是同一个人！
But it's the same bloke!

599
00:32:42,860 --> 00:32:44,420
多劲爆的大戏啊！我是说，
这才是大家爱听的玩意儿。
Such drama. I mean,
that's what you wanna hear.

600
00:32:44,460 --> 00:32:46,060
你看个节目或者听个广播，
不就图个长见识嘛！
You wanna be educated
when you watch something
or listen.

601
00:32:46,100 --> 00:32:47,900
对，我听过《阿切尔一家》。
Yeah, I listened to
The Archers.

602
00:32:47,940 --> 00:32:49,380
可拉倒吧，《阿切尔一家》
他们就光能哼哼唧唧念叨上十分钟，
No, The Archers,
they just manage to drone on
for 10 minutes

603
00:32:49,420 --> 00:32:51,660
净是讲某某人
在公共步道上溜达这种破事。
about, you know, somebody's
walk down a public footpath.

604
00:32:51,700 --> 00:32:53,340
我实在听不下去。
I just can't listen to it.

605
00:32:53,380 --> 00:32:55,980
-那就别听呗。
-我就直接关掉收音机
自己唱。
-Well, don't then.
-I just turn off the radio
and sing.

606
00:32:56,020 --> 00:32:58,740
-你听腻了《阿切尔一家》，
还有BBC二台嘛。
-对啊。
-Radio 2 is there for when
you're sick of The Archers.
-Yeah.

607
00:32:58,780 --> 00:33:01,500
不过你也可以让车流开快点啊，
放节奏快的歌就行了。
But you can speed the traffic
up as well 'cause
you can play fast records.

608
00:33:01,540 --> 00:33:03,460
-真管用。
-真的管用。
-It does work.
-It does work.

609
00:33:03,500 --> 00:33:05,140
快歌一响，
你开车也会变快吗？
Do you drive faster
when quick records come on?

610
00:33:05,180 --> 00:33:08,820
我更喜欢安静地开。
我就爱安安静静地开车。
I prefer to drive in silence.
I love to drive in silence.

611
00:33:08,860 --> 00:33:10,500
我迷恋车子引擎的轰鸣声。
I love the sound of the engine
of the car.

612
00:33:10,540 --> 00:33:12,500
这就是为什么
我买了辆野马。
And that's why
I bought a Mustang.

613
00:33:12,540 --> 00:33:15,340
因为野马是唯一一辆
听起来跟电影里一模一样的车。
'Cause a Mustang is
the only car that sounds
like it does in the films.

614
00:33:15,380 --> 00:33:20,020
还有那么几辆吧。
凯旋TR5听起来
也有点电影里的味儿。
Yeah, there's a couple.
A Triumph TR5 sounds a bit
like it does in the movies.

615
00:33:20,060 --> 00:33:21,940
但我觉着野马绝对算得上天花板了。
But I think the Mustang's
just about as good as it gets.

616
00:33:21,980 --> 00:33:25,580
-哪部电影里有TR5？
-好多电影里都有。
-What movie's a TR5 been in?
-Lots of movies.

617
00:33:25,620 --> 00:33:29,100
-[观众笑声]
-电视里也经常放。
-[AUDIENCE LAUGHS]
-On the television.

618
00:33:30,620 --> 00:33:33,660
你前阵子确实有点疯癫啊。
You did go a bit mental
a while back.

619
00:33:33,700 --> 00:33:37,180
人总得疯上一回。
非经历不可，你必须穿过那条暗道。
You got to go mental.
You have to do it. You have to
go through the tunnel.

620
00:33:37,220 --> 00:33:41,300
-你自己觉得，你到底疯到什么程度？
-哪方面？
-How mental did you go,
do you think?
-In what aspect?

621
00:33:41,340 --> 00:33:43,220
说不好。反正总能看到
关于你的各种离奇八卦。
I don't know. You just kept
reading weird stories
about you.

622
00:33:43,260 --> 00:33:44,540
噢，好吧，不过大多是真的，对吧？
Oh, well, they're gonna be
true, aren't they?

623
00:33:44,580 --> 00:33:47,540
倒也不全……好吧，是真的。
Well, they're not all that...
It's true.

624
00:33:47,580 --> 00:33:50,540
而且好多还是我自己编出来的。
I kept writing them as well.

625
00:33:50,580 --> 00:33:53,300
我记得你承认过吧，
自己之前确实有点失控脱轨了？
You have admitted, I think,
haven't you, that
you got a bit off the rails?

626
00:33:53,340 --> 00:33:55,580
对，没错，
我确实脱轨了，但我一点都不后悔。
Yeah, no,
I did go off the rails,
but I don't regret it.

627
00:33:55,620 --> 00:33:57,180
我知道我刚才调门有点飙高了，
I know my voice went
a bit high there,

628
00:33:57,220 --> 00:33:59,620
心理分析师肯定会说
我其实心里有鬼，
which psychoanalysts would say
I have a problem with it,

629
00:33:59,660 --> 00:34:02,100
[捏着假音] 但我才没有呢！
[IN FALSETTO] but I don't!

630
00:34:02,140 --> 00:34:05,100
不不，严格从这个词的意义上讲，
我现在依然处于脱轨状态。
No, no, I'm still off the
rails in that sense
of the word.

631
00:34:05,140 --> 00:34:07,020
你甚至还打起了高尔夫！
You even took up golf!

632
00:34:07,060 --> 00:34:09,700
我喜欢打高尔夫，
而且我觉得这项运动棒极了……
I like playing golf and
I think it's a great game...

633
00:34:09,740 --> 00:34:11,540
-啥玩意儿？！
